course: dictionary
lesson: 2231
title: Being afraid and being brave
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A coward is a person who is too afraid to do what is right, brave or necessary, or who runs away from danger or difficulty. Read the clues around the word. «Being frightened does not make someone a coward; courage means doing the right thing while feeling afraid.» The author says feeling afraid is normal, so a coward must be someone who lets fear stop them from doing the right thing.
explain: Calling someone a coward is also an insult. «Being frightened means you're a coward, lad.» Grandad says this, and Dad puts his fork down, because he does not agree. The sentence about being frightened is the author's clue that Grandad's idea is wrong.
explain: Look at what happens in the story. «After Connor punched Maddie's nose, half the class said «Connor's a coward, he hit a girl».» Here coward is used to say Connor has no courage to own up to what he did. A bully who picks on weaker people can be a coward too.
fact: A coward is a person who is too afraid to do what is right, brave or necessary.
fact: A coward also runs away from danger or difficulty.
fact: Being afraid is normal; acting rightly in spite of fear is bravery.
fact: «Coward» is an insult, meaning someone has no courage.
fact: «A coward's way out» means an easy choice that avoids doing what is brave or right.
exercise: «Being frightened does not make someone a coward; courage means doing the right thing while feeling afraid.» What is courage here? | Shouting at people | Never feeling scared at all | *Doing the right thing while feeling afraid | Running away fast
exercise: Grandad says «Being frightened means you're a coward, lad.» What does the first example sentence show about this idea? | It is right, because being frightened always means you are a coward | It means Grandad is a cook | *It is wrong, because being frightened is normal | It is a question about tea
exercise: After Connor punched Maddie's nose, a pupil said «Connor's a coward, he hit a girl». What does calling Connor a coward do? | It says he is the fastest runner in class | It praises him for being brave | *It insults him, saying he has no courage
exercise: The Rabbit shouts «Do as I tell you, you coward!» Which idea does coward suggest here? | Someone who loves animals | Someone who is very tall | Someone who is always on time | *Someone who is too afraid to do what is right or necessary
test: A coward runs away from ___. | a song | a birthday cake | *danger | a warm day
test: Calling someone a coward is what kind of thing? | A type of weather | A long word for a bird | *A strong insult, saying they have no courage | A kind compliment
exam: Why can a person feel afraid and still be brave? | Because being afraid is a crime | Because brave people never feel fear | Because bravery means running away | *Because acting rightly in spite of fear is bravery
